## Environment

-   Platform (select one):
    -   [x] Anthropic API
    -   [ ] AWS Bedrock
    -   [ ] Google Vertex AI
    -   [ ] Other: <!-- specify -->
-   Claude CLI version: 1.0.43 (using SDK directly)
-   Operating System: macOS 14.x
-   Terminal: N/A (using Node.js SDK)

## Bug Description

The SDK does not respect AbortController signals during query execution. When `controller.abort()` is called, the SDK continues processing and executing all queued tool calls to completion instead of stopping immediately.

## Steps to Reproduce

1. Save the following as `repro.mjs`:

```javascript
import { query } from "@anthropic-ai/claude-code/sdk.mjs";

// Minimal repro of AbortController not working
async function demonstrateBug() {
    const controller = new AbortController();
    let messageCount = 0;
    let abortedAt = null;

    console.log("Starting query that will use multiple tools...");

    try {
        for await (const message of query({
            prompt: "Create a todo list with 3 items, then read package.json, then list files in current directory",
            abortController: controller,
            options: {
                model: "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022",
                maxTurns: 10,
                permissionMode: "bypassPermissions",
            },
        })) {
            messageCount++;
            console.log(`Message ${messageCount}: ${message.type}`);

            // Abort after receiving the first assistant message
            if (message.type === "assistant" && !abortedAt) {
                abortedAt = messageCount;
                console.log(`\n>>> ABORTING at message ${messageCount} <<<`);
                console.log(`>>> controller.signal.aborted before: 
  ${controller.signal.aborted}`);
                controller.abort();
                console.log(`>>> controller.signal.aborted after: 
  ${controller.signal.aborted}`);
                console.log(`>>> Expecting query to stop soon...\n`);
            }
        }

        console.log(`\nQuery completed. Total messages: ${messageCount}`);
        console.log(`Aborted at message: ${abortedAt}`);
        console.log(`Messages after abort: ${messageCount - abortedAt}`);
    } catch (error) {
        console.log("\nQuery threw error:", error.message);
        console.log("Error name:", error.name);
    }
}

// Run the demo
demonstrateBug().catch(console.error);
```

2. Run with: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key node repro.mjs`

## Expected Behavior

When `controller.abort()` is called, the query should stop immediately and throw an AbortError:

```
Starting query that will use multiple tools...
Message 1: system
Message 2: assistant

>>> ABORTING at message 2 <<<
>>> controller.signal.aborted before: false
>>> controller.signal.aborted after: true
>>> Expecting query to stop soon...

Query threw error: The operation was aborted
Error name: AbortError
```

## Actual Behavior

The SDK continues executing all tools and completes the full query despite the abort signal:

```
Starting query that will use multiple tools...
Message 1: system
Message 2: assistant

>>> ABORTING at message 2 <<<
>>> controller.signal.aborted before:
  false
>>> controller.signal.aborted after:
  true
>>> Expecting query to stop soon...

Message 3: assistant
Message 4: assistant
Message 5: assistant
Message 6: user
Message 7: user
Message 8: user
Message 9: user
Message 10: assistant
Message 11: result

Query completed. Total messages: 11
Aborted at message: 2
Messages after abort: 9
```

## Additional Context

Tested with:

-   `@anthropic-ai/claude-code`: 1.0.43
-   `Node.js`: v18.19.0 and v20.x
